program	errors/ref_type_arg_generic_func.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	Parse error at 17:17: a generic argument may not be a reference: `&Int` is a reference, and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106; the Law of Exclusivity is statically sound only because every live reference belongs to a call still on the stack). A generic holds its argument as STORAGE — `Vector<&Int>` fills through an ordinary call argument (`v.push(&x)`) and then outlives that call — so the reference is refused here rather than at the call. Use the value type instead (`Int`), or — to reach an element the container already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141), which lends the place for a window rather than letting a pointer out
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: Parse error at 17:17: a generic argument may not be a reference: `&Int` is a reference, and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106; the Law of Exclusivity is statically sound only because every live reference belongs to a call still on the stack). A generic holds its argument as STORAGE — `Vector<&Int>` fills through an ordinary call argument (`v.push(&x)`) and then outlives that call — so the reference is refused here rather than at the call. Use the value type instead (`Int`), or — to reach an element the container already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141), which lends the place for a window rather than letting a pointer out"
